{title: I Love to Tell the Story}
{artist: Katherine Hankey / William G. Fischer}
{genre: Gospel}
{style: Traditional}
{flow: Closing}
{key: F}
{tempo: 76}
{time: 4/4}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[F]I love to tell the story of un[C7]seen things a[F]bove
Of Jesus and His glory, of [Bb]Jesus and His [F]love
I love to tell the story, be[C7]cause I know 'tis [F]true
It satisfies my longings as [Bb]nothing else can [F]do
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[F]I love to tell the story, 'twill be my theme in glory
To [C7]tell the old, old story of [F]Jesus and His love
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[F]I love to tell the story, more won[C7]derful it [F]seems
Than all the golden fancies of [Bb]all our golden [F]dreams
I love to tell the story, it [C7]did so much for [F]me
And that is just the reason I [Bb]tell it now to [F]thee
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[F]I love to tell the story, 'tis pleasant to re[C7]peat
What seems each [F]time I tell it, more [Bb]wonderfully [F]sweet
I love to tell the story, for [C7]some have never [F]heard
The message of salvation from [Bb]God's own holy [F]Word
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[F]I love to tell the story, for those who know it [C7]best
Seem hungering and [F]thirsting to hear it like the [Bb]rest
And when, in scenes of [F]glory, I sing the [C7]new, new song
'Twill be the old, old [F]story that I have [Bb]loved so [F]long
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}
